2026-11-07T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2443) 'Can the feed server's ring, store and layers carry a tick loop without a second copy of any of them?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2443) 'The repository already has the io_uring glue with a provided-buffer ring, a store that opens FoundationDB through a VFS, and layered proofs. It has no tick, no packet codec and no load generator.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2443) 'The first gate: a binary ticks at 64 Hz on Linux, sends a fixed batch of 12 entities to one registered address, and prints tick-to-send percentiles.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2443) 'EntityServer serves 64 Hz entity state beside FeedServer
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2443) 'EntityServer is a sibling of FeedServer in the same repository, built by the same lakefile (operator, 2026-11-07). It reuses the ring glue, the JWT layer and the store, and edits them where they must change. It adds no parallel copy.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2443) '- State lives in memory in a flat array. The tick path does no SQLite and no disk I/O.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2443) '- The 100 byte packet layout has one source, the entity packet contract, taken by subtree. EntityServer never re-emits the offsets.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2443) '- The tick kernel is written in a restricted Lean subset with proofs and emitted as standalone C99 with fixed-capacity arrays and no heap. The ring loop stays hand-written C.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2443) '- Pose goes by datagram. Join, leave and ownership go on a small reliable channel.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2443) '- The timer uses absolute deadlines on the monotonic clock. An overrun coalesces or drops, and never queues a backlog.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2443) '- Each client owns its own avatar entity, so pose has no write conflicts. Store writes happen behind the tick.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2443) '- RFD66606-2442, the latency metric that judges this server.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2443) '- RFD66606-2044, Lean at build time and a flat C ABI at run time.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2443) '- RFD66606-2304, the one Lean library that generates a C planner through the same compiler.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2443) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2443) 'The repository's own record was partly stale. The store path through FoundationDB, its header and the subtree are on the main branch. Parity and profile figures in the divergence notes were measured on SQLite, not on FoundationDB, and the README said the submission has no FoundationDB code.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2443) 'Rungs
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2443) '- Skateboard: timer, UDP socket, fixed batch of 12 entities, tick-to-send percentiles printed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2443) '- Multishot receive into the existing buffer ring, and a session table keyed by address.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2443) '- The codec from the contract, with two proofs: a decode reads no more than 100 bytes, and a batch with headers stays within 1,280 bytes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2443) '- Area-of-interest grid, so fan-out is users times entities in view, not users squared.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2443) '- Load generator and sweep, with a control that fails: a planted slow handler that pushes p99 over budget.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2443) '- Write-behind to the node's store, then two nodes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2443) 'Acceptance
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2443) '- The emitted C builds with strict C99 warnings as errors, and the tick object has no allocation or runtime symbols.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2443) '- Fixtures through the Lean semantics and through the emitted C give identical bytes, and a planted bug in the C makes that check fail.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2443) '- The tick kernel has zero unproved goals. No MISRA conformance is claimed.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2443) '- The default feed path keeps passing its diff and smoke scripts.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2443) '- On the CPU runner, only checks that need no cluster run. A live FoundationDB check is an integration test.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2443) 'Open
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2443) 'Extend the in-house emitter, which emits only the codec header today, or vendor the Trust-Lean compiler by subtree. One source either way, never a copy or a submodule.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2443  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-07T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2443) '- Gate evidence: the feed server, CI run 42417791013, jobs tick-budget and client sweeps (success). entity_serve.c fails a run whose p99 is over 4 ms, and the planted-defect sweeps are caught. The Lean tick kernel and its emitted-C byte check are not in the repo, so the Lean-to-C acceptance is unmet and stated as such.
 # tags: rfd:details
